User:
Please solve this issue: # Issue #1798: [FEATURE] Dont persist agent state if 
there were no updates to it

### Problem Statement

As a user of strands session manager, I would not like to persist changes to 
session if the agents state was not updated.

### Proposed Solution

Add a flag to agent state to mark that a change has been made. Then session 
manager can check if this flag is set, and use it to determine if a change 
should be pushed

### Use Case

Reduce the number of `update_agent` calls needed to be made by the session 
manager

---

## Implementation Requirements

Based on clarification discussion and repository analysis:

### Technical Approach

#### 1. Add Dirty Flag to `JSONSerializableDict`
**File:** `src/strands/types/json_dict.py`

- Add `_dirty: bool` instance attribute, initialized to `False`
- Set `_dirty = True` when `set()` is called
- Set `_dirty = True` when `delete()` is called
- Add `_is_dirty() -> bool` private method to check dirty status
- Add `_clear_dirty() -> None` private method to reset flag to `False`

> **Note:** Methods are prefixed with `_` to indicate they are internal 
implementation details for use by the session manager, not part of the public 
API.

#### 2. Modify `sync_agent()` in `RepositorySessionManager`
**File:** `src/strands/session/repository_session_manager.py`

- Track the previously synced `_internal_state` for comparison (diffing)
- Before calling `update_agent()`, check:
  - `agent.state._is_dirty()` for user-managed state changes
  - Direct comparison of current vs. previously synced `_internal_state`
- Only call `update_agent()` if either condition is true
- Clear dirty flag only **after successful sync** (keep set on failure for 
retry)
- Update tracked `_internal_state` after successful sync

### Scope Boundaries

- ✅ **In Scope:** `sync_agent()` for single `Agent` only
- ❌ **Out of Scope (future follow-up):**
  - `sync_multi_agent()` optimization
  - `sync_bidi_agent()` optimization
  - Force sync option
  - `conversation_manager_state` dirty tracking (changes infrequently)

### Files to Modify

| File | Changes |
|------|---------|
| `src/strands/types/json_dict.py` | Add `_dirty` flag, `_is_dirty()`, 
`_clear_dirty()` private methods |
| `src/strands/session/repository_session_manager.py` | Add dirty check logic in
`sync_agent()`, track internal state |
| `tests/strands/types/test_json_dict.py` | Add unit tests for dirty flag 
behavior |
| `tests/strands/session/test_repository_session_manager.py` | Add tests for 
conditional sync behavior |

### Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] `JSONSerializableDict._is_dirty()` returns `False` after initialization
- [ ] `JSONSerializableDict._is_dirty()` returns `True` after `set()` is called
- [ ] `JSONSerializableDict._is_dirty()` returns `True` after `delete()` is 
called
- [ ] `JSONSerializableDict._clear_dirty()` resets dirty flag to `False`
- [ ] `sync_agent()` skips `update_agent()` call when state is not dirty and 
internal state unchanged
- [ ] `sync_agent()` calls `update_agent()` when `agent.state` is dirty
- [ ] `sync_agent()` calls `update_agent()` when internal state has changed
- [ ] Dirty flag remains set if `update_agent()` fails (for retry on next sync)
- [ ] All existing session manager tests continue to pass
- [ ] New unit tests cover dirty flag behavior

### Additional Context

This optimization reduces unnecessary I/O operations (file writes, S3 puts, 
etc.) when the agent processes messages without modifying its state, improving 
performance especially in high-throughput scenarios.


